WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:07.300 --> 00:00:08.880
- [Mark] Okay, Levi.

00:00:08.880 --> 00:00:09.713
- Yes, sir.

00:00:09.713 --> 00:00:10.670
- [Mark] Levi, where
are you from originally?

00:00:10.670 --> 00:00:12.330
- [Levi] Orange County, Huntington Beach.

00:00:12.330 --> 00:00:13.360
- [Mark] So Orange County out here?

00:00:13.360 --> 00:00:14.240
- [Levi] Yeah.

00:00:14.240 --> 00:00:15.730
- [Mark] How long you
been here on Skid Row?

00:00:15.730 --> 00:00:18.330
- About five, six years now.

00:00:18.330 --> 00:00:20.070
- [Mark] Five, six years.

00:00:20.070 --> 00:00:21.220
Do you have family?

00:00:21.220 --> 00:00:22.737
- No, my mom just passed
away 10 years ago,

00:00:22.737 --> 00:00:24.690
and my last known relative, my uncle,

00:00:24.690 --> 00:00:26.570
passed away two years ago.

00:00:26.570 --> 00:00:27.510
So if they're out there, I don't know.

00:00:27.510 --> 00:00:30.100
It's just me, no kids, no wife, no...

00:00:30.100 --> 00:00:31.579
- [Mark] Tell me about your
childhood, what was it like?

00:00:31.579 --> 00:00:32.510
- Childhood was good, I think.

00:00:32.510 --> 00:00:36.870
My mom raised five kids
on a waitress' salary.

00:00:36.870 --> 00:00:37.900
They were all older than me.

00:00:37.900 --> 00:00:39.550
I grew up by myself in the house,

00:00:40.400 --> 00:00:42.460
my mom did whatever she
could, you know what I mean?

00:00:42.460 --> 00:00:45.346
I lived with my mom
until I was 14 years old.

00:00:45.346 --> 00:00:47.380
And then I walked in one
day, coming home from school,

00:00:47.380 --> 00:00:49.133
and my stepdad was drunk,

00:00:50.270 --> 00:00:52.973
was in the garage beating
the shit out of my mom and...

00:00:54.700 --> 00:00:57.820
Well, I went away for a
long time for that one.

00:00:57.820 --> 00:01:01.713
But, yeah, I've been here for awhile.

00:01:03.227 --> 00:01:05.010
- [Mark] And you live here on Skid Row?

00:01:05.010 --> 00:01:05.843
- Yeah.
- Where are you?

00:01:05.843 --> 00:01:07.360
- Fifth and Broadway.

00:01:07.360 --> 00:01:09.420
- So you're in a tent?
- Cardboard.

00:01:09.420 --> 00:01:10.470
- Cardboard?
- Yeah.

00:01:12.169 --> 00:01:13.734
- [Mark] Do you have a
girlfriend, anything like that?

00:01:13.734 --> 00:01:14.602
- No, just me.

00:01:14.602 --> 00:01:15.460
- No?
- Me and my bike.

00:01:15.460 --> 00:01:16.460
- [Mark] You and your bike?

00:01:16.460 --> 00:01:18.380
Very cool bike.
- Yeah, thank you.

00:01:18.380 --> 00:01:20.000
- Love your bike.
- Thank you.

00:01:21.090 --> 00:01:23.538
- [Mark] What's your
drug of choice down here?

00:01:23.538 --> 00:01:24.600
- Spice right now.

00:01:24.600 --> 00:01:25.433
- Spice?
- Yeah.

00:01:25.433 --> 00:01:26.355
- [Mark] And you've
done the other ones too?

00:01:26.355 --> 00:01:27.409
- Yeah.
- Heroin?

00:01:27.409 --> 00:01:28.379
- Yeah, I've tried heroin.

00:01:28.379 --> 00:01:29.212
I'm afraid of it

00:01:29.212 --> 00:01:31.650
because I'm too much of a drug addict.

00:01:31.650 --> 00:01:34.203
My hustle ain't, I just panhandle, so.

00:01:34.203 --> 00:01:35.610
Heroin's too expensive for me.

00:01:35.610 --> 00:01:37.640
Crystal, just run around the streets,

00:01:37.640 --> 00:01:39.370
going nowhere, so I smoke spice.

00:01:39.370 --> 00:01:40.520
It's cheaper than weed.

00:01:42.250 --> 00:01:43.487
- [Mark] So you make money by panhandling?

00:01:43.487 --> 00:01:45.050
- Panhandling. Recycling.

00:01:45.050 --> 00:01:46.590
I recycle in the morning

00:01:46.590 --> 00:01:48.490
and then I panhandle in the afternoon.

00:01:49.600 --> 00:01:51.490
Come here and eat dinner
and that's it, I'm done.

00:01:51.490 --> 00:01:52.710
- [Mark] Where do you eat?

00:01:52.710 --> 00:01:53.550
- Usually the Midnight.

00:01:53.550 --> 00:01:55.830
Or someone, I'll be panhandling
sitting by a chicken place

00:01:55.830 --> 00:01:57.137
or someone will buy me some food.

00:01:57.137 --> 00:01:58.540
But if that don't happen
I'll come down here

00:01:58.540 --> 00:01:59.373
to the Midnight.

00:02:00.740 --> 00:02:02.633
Ain't too safe at
nighttime, but it's okay.

00:02:03.880 --> 00:02:06.980
- [Mark] So, do you sell as well?

00:02:06.980 --> 00:02:08.863
- No, I don't sell, no.
- You don't sell.

00:02:10.550 --> 00:02:11.600
So tell me about sleeping here.

00:02:11.600 --> 00:02:13.063
Do you sleep here at night?

00:02:14.020 --> 00:02:15.270
- [Levi] I used to sleep right here

00:02:15.270 --> 00:02:18.790
until somebody decided to wake me up

00:02:18.790 --> 00:02:20.847
with a bright yellow crowbar
at four o'clock in the morning.

00:02:20.847 --> 00:02:21.770
- [Mark] A what?

00:02:21.770 --> 00:02:23.730
- [Levi] A bright yellow crowbar.

00:02:23.730 --> 00:02:25.280
Yeah, some Cuban dude was drunk

00:02:26.810 --> 00:02:28.810
he tried to wake me up at
four o'clock in the morning,

00:02:28.810 --> 00:02:31.370
right here on 6th and Los
Angeles with a crowbar.

00:02:31.370 --> 00:02:32.560
Luckily he dropped the crowbar

00:02:32.560 --> 00:02:33.780
so I was able to get the better him,

00:02:33.780 --> 00:02:35.680
so I don't sleep down
past Los Angeles no more

00:02:35.680 --> 00:02:38.770
I'm up towards Broadway and
Fifth by Rite Aid and stuff.

00:02:38.770 --> 00:02:41.066
In a little doorway so
the manager's cool with me

00:02:41.066 --> 00:02:42.190
as long as I clean up my mess and stuff.

00:02:42.190 --> 00:02:43.769
- [Mark] You've seen some
crazy stuff, I'm sure.

00:02:43.769 --> 00:02:46.660
- [Levi] Yeah, it's
okay to sleep by people

00:02:46.660 --> 00:02:47.670
then it's not okay, you never know

00:02:47.670 --> 00:02:49.360
when you're gonna wake up.

00:02:49.360 --> 00:02:50.460
So I sleep next to a little

00:02:50.460 --> 00:02:52.735
68-year-old woman right
now in a wheelchair.

00:02:52.735 --> 00:02:54.740
(sirens blaring)
So she does her thing

00:02:54.740 --> 00:02:55.700
during the day and then the nighttime

00:02:55.700 --> 00:02:57.180
we both go in our little cubby hole.

00:02:57.180 --> 00:02:59.580
And I get up, put her in her
in the chair in the morning

00:02:59.580 --> 00:03:01.511
and she does her thing.

00:03:01.511 --> 00:03:03.611
Down this way it could be dangerous, yeah.

00:03:06.843 --> 00:03:09.380
- [Mark] How old were you
when you started drugs?

00:03:09.380 --> 00:03:10.860
- [Levi] I was 13 years old.

00:03:10.860 --> 00:03:11.870
- 13.
- Yeah.

00:03:11.870 --> 00:03:13.224
- [Mark] What drug was that?

00:03:13.224 --> 00:03:15.900
- [Levi] My first drug was
a slam of methamphetamines

00:03:15.900 --> 00:03:17.048
from my girlfriend.

00:03:17.048 --> 00:03:18.470
14 years old.

00:03:18.470 --> 00:03:19.820
And then weed and all that.

00:03:21.400 --> 00:03:22.783
- [Mark] Have you ever been clean?

00:03:23.769 --> 00:03:24.989
- [Levi] In prison.

00:03:24.989 --> 00:03:26.869
- [Mark] What were you in prison for?

00:03:26.869 --> 00:03:28.210
- I was in prison for manslaughter

00:03:28.210 --> 00:03:29.680
when I was 14 to 21 years old.

00:03:29.680 --> 00:03:32.300
And then I've been to federal prison

00:03:32.300 --> 00:03:35.560
for manufacturing counterfeit
securities and explosives.

00:03:35.560 --> 00:03:37.150
- Wow.
- But I've been off now

00:03:37.150 --> 00:03:40.340
for five years, no probation,
no parole, nothing.

00:03:40.340 --> 00:03:43.300
- [Mark] What manslaughter?
Tell me about that.

00:03:43.300 --> 00:03:45.560
- That's when I walked home, 14 years old,

00:03:45.560 --> 00:03:48.670
and I found my step dad
beating the shit out of my mom.

00:03:48.670 --> 00:03:52.180
My mom was unconscious, she
was bleeding in the corner.

00:03:52.180 --> 00:03:53.950
I was on my way to baseball
practice so I had my bat,

00:03:53.950 --> 00:03:56.593
and I fucking hit my step
dad 38 times in the head

00:03:56.593 --> 00:03:59.130
just so he'd stop hitting my mama.

00:03:59.130 --> 00:04:01.032
I killed him.
- Wow.

00:04:01.032 --> 00:04:03.363
- They gave me juvenile life.

00:04:03.363 --> 00:04:05.233
Juvenile life for 14 to 21 years old.

00:04:13.088 --> 00:04:15.255
- [Mark] That's justified.

00:04:16.430 --> 00:04:17.593
Wow, that's heavy.

00:04:19.540 --> 00:04:21.250
Are you an only child?

00:04:21.250 --> 00:04:23.000
- I got two step brothers
and two step sisters

00:04:23.000 --> 00:04:25.610
but they were all older than
me, when I was growing up.

00:04:25.610 --> 00:04:26.443
They were out of the house.

00:04:26.443 --> 00:04:27.350
- [Mark] You were basically an only child.

00:04:27.350 --> 00:04:29.743
- Yeah.
- Wow.

00:04:30.610 --> 00:04:31.953
Thank you for sharing that.

00:04:33.460 --> 00:04:35.463
Where do you want to see
yourself in five years?

00:04:38.770 --> 00:04:39.860
- Gone.

00:04:39.860 --> 00:04:40.693
- [Mark] Gone?

00:04:45.200 --> 00:04:48.623
You have no hope for
anything brighter or? No?

00:04:51.785 --> 00:04:53.035
- I don't know.

00:04:55.060 --> 00:04:56.840
Just survive another day, you know?

00:04:56.840 --> 00:04:58.453
- [Mark] Yeah, it's hard here.

00:05:03.780 --> 00:05:05.280
Thank you for talking with me.

00:05:06.621 --> 00:05:08.204
- [Levi] Thank you.

00:05:10.080 --> 00:05:11.503
- [Mark] Good luck with everything, man.

00:05:11.503 --> 00:05:13.086
- [Levi] Thank you.

